# Context7 documentation is mandatory for external libraries

**STRICT — no exceptions.**

Before writing, editing, or reviewing any code that touches an external library, framework, SDK, API, or CLI tool (e.g. React, React Router, Vite, Salesforce SFDX/LWR, Tailwind, any npm package), you MUST:

1. Call the `context7` MCP tools (`resolve-library-id` then the docs query tool) to fetch current, real documentation for that library/version.
2. Base your usage, APIs, config, and syntax on what Context7 returns — not on prior training knowledge, memory, or assumption.
3. Do this even if you are confident you already know the API. Training data can be outdated or wrong about versions actually used in this project.

Do not skip this step for "simple" or "well-known" usage. If Context7 has no coverage for a given library, say so explicitly instead of falling back to assumed knowledge, and confirm the approach with the user before proceeding.

This rule applies to all external dependencies used anywhere under this project, including the UI Bundle (`force-app/main/default/uiBundles/`).
